From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:43:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] WayDroidService: Skip group summary notifications

When an app has several notifications, Android groups them under a
summary notification, which it adds itself (ranker_group) or the app
posts. The host's notification list doesn't group, so the summary showed
as one more notification, "Untitled notification" when Android added
it. Don't forward group summaries, as KDE Connect doesn't; each
notification in the group is still forwarded.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 .../org/lineageos/platform/internal/WayDroidService.java    | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/WayDroidService.java b/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/WayDroidService.java
index 827bf7e..d46d093 100644
--- a/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/WayDroidService.java
+++ b/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/WayDroidService.java
@@ -300,6 +300,12 @@ public class WayDroidService extends LineageSystemService {
                 String packageName = sbn.getPackageName();
                 Notification notification = sbn.getNotification();
 
+                // A group summary has little text of its own, and the desktop lists the
+                // notifications in the group one by one
+                if (notification.isGroupSummary()) {
+                    return;
+                }
+
                 if (notification.isForegroundService()) {
                     return;
                 }
-- 
